          %title The cyclic category
          %h1#the_cyclic_category The cyclic category
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#idea"} Idea
              %li
                %a{:href => "#definitions"} Definitions
              %li
                %a{:href => "#structure"} Structure of the cyclic category
              %li
                %a{:href => "#properties"} Properties
              %ul
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#general"} General
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#generalized_reedy_model_structure"} Generalized Reedy model structure
              %li
                %a{:href => "#related_concepts"} Related concepts
              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %strong cyclic category
            (
            %a{:href => "#Connes83"}> Connes 83
            , see
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Cartier85"} Cartier 85
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Λ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda
            (or sometimes
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small category
            whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaves"} presheaves
            – called
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cyclic+sets"} cyclic sets
            or more generally
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cyclic+objects"} cyclic objects
            – are somewhere intermediate between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+sets"} simplicial sets
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+sets"} symmetric sets
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplex+category"} simplex category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cyclic+groups"} cyclic groups
            for
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphism+groups"} automorphism groups
          %p
            The cycle category is used for the description of the cyclic structure on
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hochschild+homology"} Hochschild homology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hochschild+cohomology"} Hochschild cohomology
            and accordingly for the description of
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cyclic+homology"} cyclic homology
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cyclic+cohomology"} cyclic cohomology
          %h2#definitions Definitions
          %p
            Multiple descriptions of the cyclic category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Λ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda
            are possible, but a convenient starting point is to consider first a category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
            are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+numbers"} natural numbers
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ≥
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \geq 0
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-set"} hom-set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi m
                  %mo ,
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L(m, n)
            consists of increasing functions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo →
                  %mi ℤ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f: \mathbb{Z} \to \mathbb{Z}
            satisfying the “spiraling property”, that
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi i
                    %mo +
                    %mi m
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo +
                    %mi n
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(i + m + 1) = f(i) + n + 1
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
            given by ordinary function composition. The category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            is (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalent
            to) the category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Λ
                    %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda_\infty
            called the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/paracyclic+category"} paracyclic category
            by
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#NS"} Nikolaus and Scholze
          %p
            Then, define
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Λ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda
            to be a quotient category of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            having the same objects, with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Λ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi m
                  %mo ,
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi L
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi m
                  %mo ,
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mo ∼
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda(m, n) = L(m, n)/\sim
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∼
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sim
            is the equivalence relation for which
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo ∼
                  %mi g
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \sim g
            means
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo −
                  %mi g
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f - g
            is a constant multiple of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n+1
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi q
                  %mo :
                  %mi L
                  %mo →
                  %mi Λ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q: L \to \Lambda
            be the quotient.
          #simplex.num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              Notice that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi m
                    %mo ,
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \in L(m, n)
              is completely determined by the values
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ,
                      %mi …
                      %mo ,
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi m
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(0), \ldots, f(m)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/faithful+functor"} faithful
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subcategory"} embedding
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi Δ
